/fpage><lpage>234</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12049850</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><sec sec-type="display-objects"><title>Figures and Tables</title><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Fig.&#x02002;1</label><caption><p>Somatostatin-immunoreactive cells (arrow) are generally seen in the neck region of fundic glands of stomach. A control rat (<bold>1, 2</bold>), STZ-diabetic rat (<bold>3, 4</bold>), and diabetic rat given zinc sulfate (<bold>5, 6</bold>). Streptavidin-biotin-peroxidase technique (<bold>1, 3, 5</bold>), magnifications &#x000d7;200, PAS (<bold>2, 4, 6</bold>) magnifications &#x000d7;100.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="AHC05054f01"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig.&#x02002;2</label><caption><p>Somatostatin-immunoreactive cells (arrow) localized immunohistochemically in duodenum. A control rat (<bold>1, 2</bold>), STZ-diabetic rat (<bold>3, 4</bold>), and diabetic rat given zinc sulfate (<bold>5, 6</bold>). Streptavidin-biotin-peroxidase technique (<bold>1, 3, 5</bold>), magnifications &#x000d7;200, PAS (<bold>2, 4, 6</bold>), magnifications &#x000d7;100.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="AHC05054f02"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table&#x02002;1</label><caption><p>Mean levels of stomach GSH, LPO, and NEG for all groups</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Groups</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">n</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">LPO (nmol MDA&#x0002f;mg protein)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn1">&#x0002a;</xref></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">GSH (nmol GSH&#x0002f;mg protein)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn1">&#x0002a;</xref></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">NEG (nmol fructose&#x0002f;mg protein)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn1">&#x0002a;</xref></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Control</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.38&#x000b1;0.06</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">22.32&#x000b1;1.06</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">14.80&#x000b1;0.87</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Control&#x0002b;Zinc Sulfate</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.44&#x000b1;0.14<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn2">a</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">18.68&#x000b1;2.62</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">25.84&#x000b1;1.37</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diabetic</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.56&#x000b1;0.04</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">14.56&#x000b1;0.9<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn2">b</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">23.63&#x000b1;1.05<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn2">d</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diabetic&#x0002b;Zinc Sulfate</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">9</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.53&#x000b1;0.05</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">18.67&#x000b1;2.00<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn3">c</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">17.37&#x000b1;0.88<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn4">e</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">P<sub>ANOVA</sub></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0001</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0001</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0001</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tblfn1"><label>&#x0002a;</label><p> Mean&#x000b1;SD, n&#x0003d;Number of animals.</p></fn><fn id="tblfn2"><label>a, b, d</label><p> p&#x0003c;0.0001 versus control group, </p></fn><fn id="tblfn3"><label>c</label><p> p&#x0003c;0.009 versus diabetic group, </p></fn><fn id="tblfn4"><label>